<title>UK: UK Ford workers back strike ballot call.</title>
<headline>UK Ford workers back strike ballot call.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford car workers in the UK have backed a call for a national industrial action ballot over the company's plans to run-down its Halewood plant in Liverpool with the loss of 1,300 jobs, the Transport and General Workers Union said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The union said in a statement that the call had been backed by Ford workers at every plant around the country and that trade union representatives from all Ford plants would discuss holding a nationwide strike vote at a meeting in London on Thursday.</p>
<p>Last week Ford shocked its workforce by announcing 1,300 job losses out of a workforce of 4,500 at the Halewood plant in the north west of England. The plant produces Escort cars for the domestic market.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
